      "knowledge_point_id": "84355770-5926-5be6-9b9f-c13bb05599ae",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying the Horizontal Shift of a Horizontally Stretched Tangent or Cotangent Curve",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/5a58c1b6b72ab29c73457834bd093b23df234d4b161d87b026449ce18a510cb6.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/2590787ae9eed509fa2eca140078f34dc0263e5d888cb50ef81bb317896f4fa7.png) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/4a4b94629aa74d8b04caecd666b2b34f6d7a4db03b561a0207102093f3ce0366.png) is a constant. Given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/f75fd972834cbdd20e3329eee1406c25476109f66bdc63b50e65d43b495416c8.png) what is the value of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/0514151a4defc8b3e97ec86ead73038697701ead4a5999db5c16affffd20c41f.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The parameter ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/04d3d028f9f3766f1e44fb4a095a62dc92a9f16259ac8ee930254e2da0e52ae0.png) represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/23f74abe2b793b6e5d090136cafe331c5f92d4ff62df66ec94b75539259b5a6e.png)\n\nThe factor ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/2500722483533ba6dd622e9572f36ef0162889a6801352ce8f2c60f60c55167e.png) indicates that the graph of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/dd80268d579d79a6f0ca99485ec391b4034877f1f14a52fa9e6cd371cf2bfaee.png) is a horizontal translation of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/f324f716f57c696de3669f03ba36b1aa197bed1c36144777252490084c940344.png) Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/4ae5b54c0b0aafdb3e191dd01d0c3ff698bda9daee3a51ad49ecf0a0313c8186.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/a878f9eac36b11ec0a6ac3ba961c0257a9e73e872127c0167d9b64554acc84b6.png) by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/b7bbd8a714eb95c5081e7511b5b003ead8d98e0d38de8dc061d82ac15a486752.png) units to the right. Therefore,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/3bcb5d5f6e6988266fedfb0cc507aa46fdbf510e2d15ca8588253228af091621.png)\n\nSince ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/9c5ec1702df206d7f81e68ea6fbc5b795335b0b9317a4540446fe5c4235aa0bc.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/65f6e2f05e1d05f16a4f6601ebe3e49f4cb01663d31807feb5de5f6bb9e2331e.png) is in this interval, the value of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/b5c9da4fbe9c1486e2080416f6a3044a790267f9eb072ef34c164e5e12958e5c.png) is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/eef2c2e86e460a67d52eee56af496164737b41a0e2db4c1e6d4a4030b4c00167.png).",
      "difficulty": null,
